WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.110
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.380 --> 01:34.910
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.210 --> 01:37.680
[Episode 26]

4
01:38.410 --> 01:39.350
Zhou Hunyuan reports by telegram:

5
01:39.350 --> 01:40.070
So far,

6
01:40.220 --> 01:43.280
[Fan Shaozeng's Residence, Chongqing]

7
01:40.360 --> 01:42.009
the Communist army shows no sign of retreating.

8
01:42.009 --> 01:43.940
Their assault is growing fiercer.

9
01:43.990 --> 01:44.950
Order the air force

10
01:44.950 --> 01:46.009
to send more planes

11
01:46.370 --> 01:47.430
to step up support.

12
01:47.430 --> 01:47.990
Yes, sir.

13
01:50.350 --> 01:52.160
Where are the rest of our forces now?

14
01:52.160 --> 01:52.920
Map.

15
01:53.850 --> 01:56.539
Wu Qiwei's 2 divisions are at Fengxiangba,

16
01:57.229 --> 01:58.200
where they've been under enemy attack

17
01:58.200 --> 01:59.640
for nearly 5 hours.

18
01:59.870 --> 02:02.470
They have now detoured to support Lubanchang.

19
02:02.730 --> 02:04.190
Guo Xunqi's unit of the Sichuan Army

20
02:04.190 --> 02:05.450
has moved from Lianghekou

21
02:05.450 --> 02:07.730
towards Tanchang and Lubanchang.

22
02:08.449 --> 02:09.720
The fastest-moving unit right now

23
02:09.720 --> 02:12.010
is He Zhizhong's 1st Division of the Guizhou Army.

24
02:12.010 --> 02:13.550
He has followed the main force of the Communist army

25
02:13.550 --> 02:15.010
to the Yong'an Temple area.

26
02:15.010 --> 02:15.670
All these units

27
02:15.670 --> 02:17.030
will soon form an encirclement

28
02:17.030 --> 02:18.430
to annihilate the enemy in Lubanchang.

29
02:18.430 --> 02:19.770
This time, as long as Zhou Hunyuan

30
02:19.770 --> 02:21.430
can resist the Communist army's offensive,

31
02:21.430 --> 02:23.230
a great victory can be achieved.

32
02:23.380 --> 02:25.710
This time Zhou Hunyuan is quite resolute.

33
02:26.430 --> 02:28.120
A great victory can be achieved.

34
02:28.120 --> 02:30.640
His pursuit of them all the way

35
02:30.670 --> 02:32.530
from Jiangxi to here was worth it.

36
02:35.430 --> 02:37.829
There's just one thing I don't understand.

37
02:38.280 --> 02:39.690
What are you worried about?

38
02:39.690 --> 02:43.020
Mao Zedong has always been cunning in his military tactics.

39
02:44.630 --> 02:47.829
Why is he

40
02:49.260 --> 02:51.980
so reckless this time?

41
02:58.450 --> 03:02.850
Is the Communist army really at a dead end?

42
03:05.440 --> 03:12.350
[Tanchang, Renhuai, Guizhou]

43
03:25.930 --> 03:26.730
Leaders.

44
03:27.170 --> 03:30.170
The Second Bureau just deciphered an enemy telegram.

45
03:30.560 --> 03:34.360
The Guizhou Army, Sichuan Army, and Central Army are all closing in.

46
03:35.390 --> 03:36.940
What's the situation in Lubanchang?

47
03:36.940 --> 03:38.280
The battle is still ongoing.

48
03:38.280 --> 03:39.450
Zhou Hunyuan has concentrated his troops

49
03:39.450 --> 03:40.760
in the central area.

50
03:41.560 --> 03:42.960
Relying on air cover,

51
03:43.180 --> 03:44.420
they are fighting to the death.

52
03:44.420 --> 03:47.220
Many positions have changed hands several times.

53
03:50.720 --> 03:51.440
Mao.

54
03:52.000 --> 03:53.060
Should we consider

55
03:53.079 --> 03:55.610
letting Lin and Nie withdraw from the battle?

56
04:04.730 --> 04:06.130
The time is not right yet.

57
04:07.790 --> 04:09.410
Is there a telegram from Lin and Nie?

58
04:09.410 --> 04:10.040
Not yet.

59
04:44.190 --> 04:47.070
[Headquarters of the 1st Red Army Corps, Lubanchang, Renhuai, Guizhou]

60
04:46.330 --> 04:47.159
How's the situation?

61
04:47.159 --> 04:50.220
[Lin Biao, Commander of the 1st Red Army Corps]

62
04:47.680 --> 04:49.940
The enemy shows no signs of collapse yet.

63
04:49.940 --> 04:51.010
On our attack route,

64
04:50.750 --> 04:53.890
[Zuo Quan, Chief of Staff of the 1st Red Army Corps]

65
04:51.040 --> 04:52.780
there are many woods and narrow paths.

66
04:52.780 --> 04:54.130
Our troops can't deploy.

67
04:54.130 --> 04:55.590
And we lack heavy weapons.

68
04:55.640 --> 04:58.120
It's hard to break through to the enemy's core fortress area.

69
04:58.120 --> 04:59.750
It seems we need to be prepared

70
04:59.750 --> 05:01.410
for a standoff with the enemy.

71
05:02.340 --> 05:03.510
The enemy can afford to wait.

72
05:03.510 --> 05:05.510
But can we?

73
05:05.460 --> 05:07.570
[Nie Rongzhen, Political Commissar of the 1st Red Army Corps]

74
05:05.840 --> 05:07.170
What are your thoughts?

75
05:07.420 --> 05:09.280
The Front Command didn't give us a strict order.

76
05:09.280 --> 05:10.430
If we can win, we fight.

77
05:10.430 --> 05:11.190
If not,

78
05:12.000 --> 05:12.920
we leave.

79
05:13.990 --> 05:15.540
If we wait for the enemy's reinforcements,

80
05:15.540 --> 05:17.040
we won't be able to leave even if we want to.

81
05:17.040 --> 05:18.130
Send a telegram to the Front Command.

82
05:18.130 --> 05:18.810
Suggest

83
05:19.190 --> 05:21.250
the troops withdraw from the battle.

84
05:21.840 --> 05:22.900
Send the telegram.

85
05:23.690 --> 05:24.890
Hurry, hurry, hurry.

86
05:35.350 --> 05:36.950
Come, everyone have a taste.

87
05:36.970 --> 05:37.570
Okay.

88
05:41.320 --> 05:42.520
I'll have a taste too.

89
05:53.520 --> 05:55.830
The telegram from Lin and Nie has arrived.

90
05:55.830 --> 05:56.720
What does it say?

91
05:56.720 --> 05:57.610
They suggest

92
05:58.170 --> 06:00.500
withdrawing from the Lubanchang battle.

93
06:04.370 --> 06:05.660
Lin Biao's thinking

94
06:06.050 --> 06:07.200
is in line with ours.

95
06:09.300 --> 06:11.960
If we continue this business, we'll lose money.

96
06:12.630 --> 06:14.360
Then let's make a prompt decision.

97
06:14.360 --> 06:15.360
Approve their suggestion.

98
06:15.360 --> 06:16.600
Withdraw from the battle.

99
06:16.600 --> 06:19.950
The main force will transfer towards Renhuai and Maotai.

100
06:20.830 --> 06:21.430
Also,

101
06:23.010 --> 06:24.080
order the 1st Corps

102
06:25.090 --> 06:28.180
to send the training battalion and 2 engineer companies.

103
06:28.180 --> 06:30.210
They must, before dawn tomorrow,

104
06:30.600 --> 06:33.400
rush to the section between Maotai and Xiaohekou,

105
06:33.580 --> 06:34.850
and build 3 pontoon bridges.

106
06:34.850 --> 06:36.360
Have them ready by tomorrow,

107
06:36.360 --> 06:38.520
and ensure the safety around the pontoon bridges.

108
06:38.520 --> 06:39.120
Okay.

109
06:39.870 --> 06:40.930
I'll go over first.

110
06:48.760 --> 06:51.960
We are going to cross the Chishui River for the third time.

111
06:53.330 --> 06:53.930
Yes.

112
06:54.900 --> 06:56.350
When we reach Maotai Town,

113
06:56.350 --> 06:58.390
we will immediately issue the order to cross the river.

114
06:58.390 --> 07:00.920
All Corps and the Military Commission Column

115
07:01.000 --> 07:02.480
must, between the evening of the 16th

116
07:02.480 --> 07:03.790
and 12:00 on the 17th,

117
07:03.840 --> 07:06.500
all arrive at the west bank of the Chishui River,

118
07:06.600 --> 07:08.900
and then seek strategic maneuverability.

119
07:08.900 --> 07:09.630
In addition,

120
07:09.970 --> 07:12.170
the order must clearly inform all Corps

121
07:12.290 --> 07:14.080
not to stop after crossing the Chishui River,

122
07:14.080 --> 07:15.940
but to continue west or northwest

123
07:15.970 --> 07:17.360
for 10 to 15 kilometers

124
07:18.190 --> 07:20.650
before taking cover and resting on the spot.

125
07:21.170 --> 07:22.020
Mao,

126
07:22.250 --> 07:24.510
you are so afraid that the Generalissimo

127
07:24.850 --> 07:26.250
will make a misjudgment.

128
07:26.860 --> 07:27.790
I have no choice.

129
07:28.210 --> 07:30.420
The Generalissimo is suspicious by nature.

130
07:30.420 --> 07:31.880
I'm afraid he can't sleep.

131
07:32.090 --> 07:33.350
We march 15 kilometers

132
07:33.810 --> 07:35.740
just to report to the Generalissimo

133
07:35.740 --> 07:38.870
that we are going to cross the Yangtze River to the north.

134
07:38.980 --> 07:41.180
You've really racked your brains for him.

135
07:41.180 --> 07:41.940
This time,

136
07:42.330 --> 07:44.860
we must break out of Chiang Kai-shek's encirclement

137
07:44.860 --> 07:47.190
and leave their troops behind to the east.

138
07:48.060 --> 07:49.130
Just as Mao said,

139
07:49.180 --> 07:52.180
from facing enemies on all sides to facing them on one side,

140
07:52.180 --> 07:54.710
the enemies have all run to northern Guizhou,

141
07:54.860 --> 07:56.720
leaving southern Sichuan empty.

142
07:59.360 --> 08:01.280
How are my broad beans roasted?

143
08:01.810 --> 08:02.990
Crispy and fragrant.

144
08:02.990 --> 08:04.250
The heat is just right.

145
08:05.250 --> 08:08.380
How does it compare to the roasted broad beans in Yunnan?

146
08:09.180 --> 08:10.660
Compared to when I was in Yunnan,

147
08:10.660 --> 08:11.990
it's just as delicious.

148
08:13.500 --> 08:14.740
What other delicious food is there in Yunnan?

149
08:14.740 --> 08:15.740
There are so many.

150
08:16.200 --> 08:18.030
There's Xuanwei ham,

151
08:18.210 --> 08:19.540
small pot rice noodles,

152
08:23.180 --> 08:24.130
and fish mint.

153
08:42.260 --> 08:43.210
Reporting, Commander.

154
08:43.210 --> 08:44.660
We have scouted everywhere.

155
08:44.660 --> 08:45.900
The Communist army that fought us last night

156
08:45.900 --> 08:46.900
has completely disappeared,

157
08:46.900 --> 08:48.900
and their whereabouts are unknown.

158
08:51.490 --> 08:52.150
Commander.

159
08:52.200 --> 08:53.930
Should we send pursuit troops?

160
08:54.060 --> 08:54.900
Didn't he just say

161
08:54.900 --> 08:55.990
the Communist army's whereabouts are unknown?

162
08:55.990 --> 08:57.590
Where should we pursue them?

163
08:57.790 --> 08:58.850
But if the higher-ups ask,

164
08:58.850 --> 08:59.800
how should we answer?

165
08:59.800 --> 09:01.400
Do they have the nerve to ask?

166
09:01.690 --> 09:03.830
We fought alone in Lubanchang,

167
09:04.060 --> 09:05.290
holding back the Communist army for a day and a night.

168
09:05.290 --> 09:07.730
It was already hard enough to hold the position.

169
09:07.730 --> 09:08.970
The friendly forces failed to reinforce us effectively,

170
09:08.970 --> 09:09.950
causing the Communist army to escape.

171
09:09.950 --> 09:11.590
What does it have to do with me?

172
09:11.590 --> 09:12.920
If we attack rashly now,

173
09:13.140 --> 09:14.180
what if we fall into the Communist army's

174
09:14.180 --> 09:16.240
feigned retreat and counterattack?

175
09:16.660 --> 09:17.460
Don't forget,

176
09:17.890 --> 09:19.490
a few days ago they racked their brains

177
09:19.490 --> 09:20.750
to lure me out to fight.

178
09:20.940 --> 09:22.000
You are right, sir.

179
09:24.790 --> 09:25.790
Pass on my order.

180
09:27.090 --> 09:28.810
Order all units to hold their positions.

181
09:28.810 --> 09:31.210
No unauthorized movement without orders,

182
09:31.380 --> 09:33.690
in case the Communist army makes a comeback.

183
09:33.690 --> 09:34.390
Yes, sir.

184
09:43.090 --> 09:45.850
From the evening of March 16, 1935,

185
09:45.850 --> 09:48.450
to 12:00 noon on March 17,

186
09:49.420 --> 09:51.300
the Military Commission Column of the Central Red Army

187
09:51.000 --> 09:55.120
[Maotai Ferry,Renhuai, Guizhou]

188
09:51.300 --> 09:53.080
and its main Corps

189
09:53.420 --> 09:56.330
crossed the Chishui River from east to west in turn,

190
09:56.350 --> 09:59.880
historically known as the Third Crossing of the Chishui River.

191
10:00.490 --> 10:02.140
Chiang is so angry he keeps sighing.

192
10:02.140 --> 10:04.260
He's dizzy and has no idea what to do.

193
10:07.470 --> 10:08.200
Xie Xingguo.

194
10:08.900 --> 10:09.690
Chairman.

195
10:09.880 --> 10:11.480
Let me add a few lines for you.

196
10:11.810 --> 10:14.410
Chiang is so angry he keeps sighing.

197
10:14.530 --> 10:16.380
Frowning and shaking his head.

198
10:16.510 --> 10:18.400
Staring and stomping his feet.

199
10:18.560 --> 10:19.250
Okay.

200
10:21.550 --> 10:22.430
Xie Xingguo.

201
10:22.710 --> 10:23.990
I heard from Zhu Rui

202
10:24.230 --> 10:26.490
about your story of chasing our Red Army.

203
10:26.490 --> 10:27.870
Do you know how many miles

204
10:27.870 --> 10:28.750
you've walked?

205
10:32.260 --> 10:34.140
Chairman, I don't know.

206
10:35.490 --> 10:37.140
Then let me calculate it for you.

207
10:37.140 --> 10:38.600
Where did you fall behind?

208
10:38.970 --> 10:39.810
Slow down.

209
10:40.810 --> 10:43.690
I was scattered by the enemy

210
10:43.690 --> 10:44.850
at the Xiang River.

211
10:45.060 --> 10:45.970
Xiang River.

212
10:46.130 --> 10:48.090
Were you on the east bank or the west bank of the Xiang River?

213
10:48.090 --> 10:49.380
You have to include the distance

214
10:49.380 --> 10:50.580
across the river too.

215
10:50.900 --> 10:51.660
Be careful.

216
10:51.970 --> 10:52.770
Enemy planes!

217
10:53.020 --> 10:53.660
Enemy planes incoming!

218
10:53.660 --> 10:54.380
Enemy planes!

219
10:54.380 --> 10:55.780
Chairman, enemy planes.

220
10:55.810 --> 10:56.450
Be careful!

221
10:56.450 --> 10:56.970
Hurry!

222
10:57.380 --> 10:58.450
Hurry up!

223
10:58.450 --> 10:59.730
Keep up!

224
11:01.020 --> 11:01.780
Be careful!

225
11:31.490 --> 11:32.290
Chairman Mao.

226
11:32.430 --> 11:33.380
Can we organize firepower

227
11:33.380 --> 11:34.520
to take down an enemy plane?

228
11:34.520 --> 11:36.100
Is this enemy plane scouting us?

229
11:36.100 --> 11:36.590
Yes, sir.

230
11:36.590 --> 11:38.330
Is it strafing us with machine guns?

231
11:38.330 --> 11:38.730
Yes, sir.

232
11:38.730 --> 11:39.460
Then why ask?

233
11:39.810 --> 11:40.490
Take it down.

234
11:40.490 --> 11:41.540
Yes, take it down.

235
11:41.780 --> 11:42.940
Ye Yinting, let's go.

236
11:42.940 --> 11:44.330
Machine Gun Company, follow me.

237
11:44.330 --> 11:45.060
Yes, sir.

238
11:46.300 --> 11:46.970
Stay safe.

239
11:47.450 --> 11:48.000
Chairman.

240
11:48.000 --> 11:49.460
Chairman Mao, for safety,

241
11:49.540 --> 11:50.490
let's move further inside.

242
11:50.490 --> 11:50.950
No need.

243
11:51.020 --> 11:52.620
Sit down, everyone sit down.

244
11:53.210 --> 11:53.570
Sit.

245
11:53.570 --> 11:54.500
Winter boy, sit.

246
11:54.810 --> 11:55.690
Come, sit.

247
11:58.900 --> 11:59.570
Winter boy.

248
12:00.020 --> 12:01.260
Did you get your share of the liquor?

249
12:01.260 --> 12:01.940
I did.

250
12:02.080 --> 12:03.380
I also bought some myself.

251
12:03.380 --> 12:04.610
But please rest assured, Chairman Mao.

252
12:04.610 --> 12:05.470
It won't delay things.

253
12:05.470 --> 12:06.310
I'm reluctant to drink it.

254
12:06.310 --> 12:07.670
Just a small sip a day.

255
12:08.210 --> 12:10.100
You built those pontoon bridges very well.

256
12:10.100 --> 12:11.150
They're even stronger than the ones

257
12:11.150 --> 12:12.150
at the Yudu River.

258
12:12.450 --> 12:13.260
Winter boy.

259
12:13.570 --> 12:14.400
Do you remember the 4 pontoon bridges we built

260
12:14.400 --> 12:16.590
when we crossed the Chishui River

261
12:16.850 --> 12:18.140
for the second time?

262
12:18.380 --> 12:19.040
I remember.

263
12:19.450 --> 12:20.660
At Lintan, Erlangtan,

264
12:20.660 --> 12:21.980
Taipingdu, and Jiuxikou.

265
12:21.980 --> 12:24.090
Chairman Mao, why are you asking about this?

266
12:24.090 --> 12:25.970
Wang Yaonan, send someone immediately

267
12:25.970 --> 12:27.810
to check the pontoon bridges at these places.

268
12:27.810 --> 12:28.570
If the bridges are still there,

269
12:28.570 --> 12:29.690
have them guarded immediately

270
12:29.690 --> 12:30.490
and report to me at once.

271
12:30.490 --> 12:31.710
Yes, I'll send someone right away.

272
12:31.710 --> 12:32.190
Go.

273
12:33.110 --> 12:33.790
Bocheng.

274
12:41.490 --> 12:42.420
It was shot down!

275
12:44.210 --> 12:45.090
It fell!

276
12:45.780 --> 12:46.660
Great!

277
12:47.210 --> 12:49.180
-Great. -It's a pity two got away.

278
12:50.180 --> 12:51.090
It's not a pity.

279
12:51.730 --> 12:54.140
They can go back and report to Generalissimo Chiang.

280
12:54.140 --> 12:55.900
Our soldiers are really doing us proud,

281
12:55.900 --> 12:57.970
shooting down planes with every shot.

282
12:57.970 --> 13:00.170
Chiang is crying and stomping his feet,

283
13:00.180 --> 13:02.180
tears and snot all over the floor.

284
13:02.180 --> 13:04.660
Tears and snot all over the floor.

285
13:05.140 --> 13:05.730
Good!

286
13:05.730 --> 13:09.900
Good, good, good.

287
13:10.090 --> 13:11.180
The third crossing of the Chishui River

288
13:11.180 --> 13:13.310
confused Chiang Kai-shek for a while.

289
13:13.450 --> 13:16.570
He raised questions in his diary for 3 consecutive days.

290
13:16.570 --> 13:18.090
On March 16, he wrote,

291
13:18.380 --> 13:21.850
"The 'bandits' fled west from Maotai, then turned south,

292
13:21.850 --> 13:22.660
then north.

293
13:23.140 --> 13:25.350
Did they leave a part in the east?"

294
13:25.890 --> 13:27.090
On the 17th, he wrote,

295
13:27.380 --> 13:29.850
"Did the 'bandits' really flee west to Gulin?"

296
13:29.850 --> 13:31.050
On the 18th, he wrote,

297
13:31.140 --> 13:33.610
"The 'bandits' are fleeing towards the southeast of Gulin.

298
13:33.610 --> 13:36.810
Will they cross the Chishui River south and flee west?"

299
13:37.400 --> 13:40.090
The Red Army went west, south, north, and stayed east.

300
13:40.090 --> 13:41.350
He mentioned them all,

301
13:41.590 --> 13:44.080
obviously losing his judgment for a while.

302
13:44.380 --> 13:45.640
What comforted him was

303
13:45.730 --> 13:47.540
that the strategy of using one enemy to destroy another,

304
13:47.540 --> 13:49.200
implemented by pursuing the Red Army,

305
13:49.200 --> 13:51.510
was finally realized in Guizhou.

306
13:51.570 --> 13:53.660
The Zhu-Mao Communist army's frantic fleeing

307
13:53.660 --> 13:54.660
back to southern Sichuan

308
13:54.660 --> 13:56.530
is nothing more than an undecided strategic policy.

309
13:56.530 --> 13:58.210
Failing to cross the Wujiang River to the east,

310
13:58.210 --> 13:59.790
they want to cross the Yangtze River to the north

311
13:59.790 --> 14:01.520
to join Xu Xiangqian's troops.

312
14:01.830 --> 14:04.060
Southern Sichuan is cold and lacks food,

313
14:04.060 --> 14:05.900
plus it's sparsely populated

314
14:06.060 --> 14:07.210
and the language is a barrier.

315
14:07.210 --> 14:08.090
It's too difficult for the Communist army

316
14:08.090 --> 14:09.060
to survive there

317
14:09.420 --> 14:10.280
for a long time.

318
14:10.480 --> 14:12.730
As long as we can hold the natural barrier of the Yangtze River,

319
14:12.730 --> 14:15.210
they will be a dead piece in southern Sichuan.

320
14:15.210 --> 14:16.810
Right. We should send more planes to scout

321
14:16.810 --> 14:18.420
and keep a close eye on their every move.

322
14:18.420 --> 14:20.940
Since the Communist army has already fled west,

323
14:20.940 --> 14:22.140
the matter in Guizhou

324
14:22.730 --> 14:24.610
should be settled.

325
14:26.320 --> 14:28.140
As you expected, Generalissimo,

326
14:28.140 --> 14:29.910
Wang Jialie has basically agreed

327
14:29.910 --> 14:32.330
to resign as the chairman of Guizhou Province.

328
14:32.330 --> 14:33.810
But he made a request

329
14:34.320 --> 14:35.300
to keep his position

330
14:35.300 --> 14:37.180
as Commander of the 25th Army,

331
14:37.760 --> 14:40.880
and hopes the government can guarantee military pay.

332
14:41.180 --> 14:42.660
I heard the 25th Army is making a fuss

333
14:42.660 --> 14:44.060
because of unpaid wages.

334
14:44.970 --> 14:45.520
The Generalissimo

335
14:45.520 --> 14:47.250
has actually considered this.

336
14:47.450 --> 14:49.720
I will soon go to western Guizhou

337
14:49.900 --> 14:52.420
to meet He Zhizhong, Commander of the 1st Division of the Guizhou Army,

338
14:52.420 --> 14:54.420
and Bai Huizhang, Commander of the 2nd Division,

339
14:54.420 --> 14:55.280
to pacify them.

340
14:55.540 --> 14:57.810
The Generalissimo is indeed far-sighted.

341
14:57.810 --> 14:58.900
The Guizhou matter

342
14:59.610 --> 15:00.730
should be worry-free now.

343
15:00.730 --> 15:01.290
Good.

344
15:15.040 --> 15:22.060
[Guiyang, Guizhou]

345
15:15.260 --> 15:16.690
Pack up. Hurry up.

346
15:17.660 --> 15:17.970
You,

347
15:18.090 --> 15:18.850
pack up.

348
15:19.020 --> 15:20.140
If you don't, I'll smash it.

349
15:20.140 --> 15:21.210
Move faster.

350
15:21.540 --> 15:22.160
Pack up.

351
15:23.490 --> 15:25.210
Stop talking nonsense. Pack up quickly.

352
15:25.210 --> 15:25.870
Put it away.

353
15:26.180 --> 15:26.490
You,

354
15:26.660 --> 15:27.590
go back quickly.

355
15:28.260 --> 15:29.210
Pack up.

356
15:29.610 --> 15:30.490
Hurry. Pack up.

357
15:30.690 --> 15:31.180
Okay.

358
15:31.180 --> 15:32.570
Pack up quickly.

359
15:32.780 --> 15:34.210
Go.

360
15:34.210 --> 15:34.870
Go quickly.

361
15:35.090 --> 15:36.300
Close the stall. Hurry up.

362
15:36.300 --> 15:37.060
Sir. Sir.

363
15:37.540 --> 15:38.380
Sit down and have a bowl of rice noodles.

364
15:38.380 --> 15:40.060
Just pack up when told. Stop talking nonsense.

365
15:40.060 --> 15:41.060
Okay. Right away.

366
15:41.450 --> 15:42.570
Just pack up when told.

367
15:42.570 --> 15:44.570
If you say one more word, I'll smash everything.

368
15:44.570 --> 15:45.630
Can't they close up

369
15:46.840 --> 15:47.650
a bit later?

370
15:48.440 --> 15:49.890
Are you tired of living?

371
15:50.260 --> 15:51.590
Can't you speak nicely?

372
15:54.270 --> 15:56.270
Why do they have to close the stalls?

373
15:57.780 --> 15:59.240
Are you pushing your luck?

374
16:01.970 --> 16:04.900
Director Xue of our Guizhou Pacification Commissioner's Office

375
16:04.900 --> 16:05.940
is passing by here

376
16:05.780 --> 16:09.090
[Wang Jialie, Commander of the Kuomintang’s 25th Army, Chairman of the Guizhou Provincial Government]

377
16:06.300 --> 16:08.590
to conduct a major inspection for the New Life Movement.

378
16:08.590 --> 16:10.850
This is his first time patrolling the streets,

379
16:10.850 --> 16:12.620
so of course there's martial law.

380
16:12.620 --> 16:14.540
Sir, please cooperate.

381
16:14.810 --> 16:15.780
Finish eating and leave quickly.

382
16:15.780 --> 16:16.300
Pack up.

383
16:16.350 --> 16:18.710
Sir, close the stall as soon as they finish eating.

384
16:18.710 --> 16:19.350
Hurry up.

385
16:19.370 --> 16:20.300
Pack up quickly.

386
16:20.450 --> 16:21.800
Didn't you hear us tell you to pack up quickly?

387
16:21.800 --> 16:22.330
Hurry up.

388
16:35.300 --> 16:35.940
Pack up.

389
16:36.900 --> 16:37.540
Pack up.

390
16:37.570 --> 16:38.780
You, pack up.

391
16:40.330 --> 16:40.970
Pack up.

392
16:41.020 --> 16:41.660
Hurry up.

393
16:42.850 --> 16:43.780
Pack up quickly.

394
17:14.609 --> 17:15.480
Grandma.

395
17:15.849 --> 17:17.329
Hurry, let's go!

396
17:18.440 --> 17:19.089
Hurry up.

397
17:20.140 --> 17:20.690
Pack up quickly.

398
17:20.690 --> 17:21.349
Put it away.

399
17:21.359 --> 17:22.960
Put everything away. Hurry.

400
17:23.180 --> 17:24.210
Get up quickly.

401
17:35.080 --> 17:36.760
In the spring of 1935,

402
17:37.420 --> 17:40.100
under Chiang Kai-shek's internal and external attacks

403
17:40.100 --> 17:41.700
and coercion from all sides,

404
17:42.190 --> 17:46.100
Wang Jialie successively resigned as Chairman of the Kuomintang Guizhou Provincial Government

405
17:46.100 --> 17:47.830
and Commander of the 25th Army.

406
17:48.530 --> 17:49.660
The King of Guizhou, who was once supported

407
17:49.660 --> 17:51.640
by Chiang Kai-shek,

408
17:51.830 --> 17:55.710
completely lost control of Guizhou from then on.

409
17:55.970 --> 17:57.100
In 1949,

410
17:57.510 --> 18:00.590
shortly after the Chinese PLA liberated Guizhou,

411
18:01.000 --> 18:02.870
Wang Jialie, who was living in retirement in his hometown,

412
18:02.870 --> 18:06.310
cooperated with the People's Government to take over the regime.

413
18:06.310 --> 18:09.660
He was appointed as a member of the Southwest Military and Political Committee,

414
18:09.660 --> 18:12.450
and later served as Vice Chairman of the Guizhou Provincial Committee of the CPPCC.

415
18:12.450 --> 18:16.250
He died of illness in Guiyang in August 1966.

416
18:19.940 --> 18:31.030
[Mountainous Region of Southern Sichuan]

417
18:31.860 --> 18:32.660
Red Army.

418
18:32.690 --> 18:34.420
How do you pronounce this word?

419
18:34.620 --> 18:35.380
Wis...

420
18:35.580 --> 18:37.210
I don't know that part below.

421
18:37.580 --> 18:38.250
dom.

422
18:38.580 --> 18:39.140
dom.

423
18:39.530 --> 18:40.490
Wisdom.

424
18:40.770 --> 18:41.620
Wisdom.

425
18:42.340 --> 18:42.740
Right.

426
18:42.860 --> 18:43.620
Wisdom.

427
18:44.090 --> 18:45.020
Red Army.

428
18:47.550 --> 18:48.790
Battle.

429
18:52.150 --> 18:52.990
Fight.

430
18:55.100 --> 18:55.940
Fight.

431
18:57.120 --> 18:58.250
Company Commander.

432
18:58.340 --> 18:59.340
[Mao Zhenhua, Company Commander of the 3rd Company, 1st Battalion, 4th Regiment]

433
18:58.530 --> 18:59.570
Company Commander Mao.

434
18:59.570 --> 19:00.520
What's wrong again?

435
19:00.520 --> 19:01.430
This word.

436
19:01.740 --> 19:03.470
How do you pronounce this word?

437
19:06.600 --> 19:08.630
I just told you. You forgot again.

438
19:09.490 --> 19:11.340
This word is too weird. I can't remember it.

439
19:11.340 --> 19:12.210
"Circle,"

440
19:12.510 --> 19:14.340
as in going around in circles.

441
19:14.940 --> 19:16.620
Read it a few more times and you'll get it.

442
19:16.620 --> 19:17.290
Circle.

443
19:17.620 --> 19:19.020
Going around in circles.

444
19:19.620 --> 19:20.490
Circle.

445
19:22.450 --> 19:23.850
Going around in circles.

446
19:23.970 --> 19:24.580
Circle.

447
19:25.860 --> 19:28.250
Circle. Going around in circles.

448
19:33.420 --> 19:35.050
Kid, watch your step.

449
19:39.820 --> 19:40.900
Comrades,

450
19:41.690 --> 19:42.730
watch your step!

451
19:43.140 --> 19:44.210
If anyone falls,

452
19:44.690 --> 19:45.860
help each other out.

453
21:37.830 --> 21:38.760
Okay, slow down.

454
21:42.380 --> 21:43.880
Is that you two, Bocheng and Jiaxiang?

455
21:43.880 --> 21:44.900
Commander-in-Chief.

456
21:44.900 --> 21:45.830
Did you fall too?

457
21:46.340 --> 21:47.140
I didn't fall.

458
21:47.210 --> 21:48.810
The stretcher-bearer fell.

459
21:49.030 --> 21:50.210
He went to help the stretcher-bearer,

460
21:50.210 --> 21:51.670
and I ended up falling too.

461
21:54.320 --> 21:55.080
Look.

462
21:57.210 --> 21:58.340
That beard leaves no doubt.

463
21:58.340 --> 21:59.740
It's Vice Chairman Zhou.

464
22:01.530 --> 22:03.390
I saw his stretcher-bearer fall,

465
22:03.450 --> 22:04.490
and ran over quickly,

466
22:04.490 --> 22:06.420
and ended up falling like this too.

467
22:06.940 --> 22:08.100
It seems that among us,

468
22:08.100 --> 22:09.070
only Mao is fine.

469
22:10.900 --> 22:12.230
The horse is very clean.

470
22:19.820 --> 22:22.150
Chairman, how did you end up like this too?

471
22:23.060 --> 22:24.720
I saw you all fall one by one.

472
22:25.050 --> 22:26.420
How could I not fall?

473
22:27.100 --> 22:28.230
Hurry up and come in.

474
22:30.150 --> 22:30.770
When we set off,

475
22:30.770 --> 22:32.750
we were all clean-shaven scholars.

476
22:32.750 --> 22:33.820
Now, one by one,

477
22:34.010 --> 22:35.740
we're all painted-face roles.

478
22:36.450 --> 22:37.180
I think,

479
22:37.420 --> 22:40.210
Generalissimo Chiang's bounty won't be given out.

480
22:40.210 --> 22:40.770
Look.

481
22:40.970 --> 22:42.340
With our looks,

482
22:42.420 --> 22:44.450
even if Generalissimo Chiang stood here,

483
22:44.450 --> 22:45.910
he wouldn't recognize us.

484
22:46.910 --> 22:48.170
Go get a basin of water.

485
22:48.770 --> 22:49.770
Comrade Bocheng.

486
22:49.940 --> 22:51.340
How is the situation now?

487
22:52.050 --> 22:52.860
Leaders.

488
22:53.180 --> 22:54.490
The comrades sent to Erlangtan

489
22:54.490 --> 22:56.530
and Taipingdu reported back that

490
22:56.820 --> 22:57.690
the 2 pontoon bridges

491
22:57.690 --> 22:59.940
were well protected by the locals.

492
23:00.290 --> 23:01.440
With a little reinforcement,

493
23:01.440 --> 23:04.100
they can be used by our troops to cross the river.

494
23:04.730 --> 23:05.420
Great.

495
23:05.660 --> 23:06.940
Any changes in the enemy's situation?

496
23:06.940 --> 23:08.420
According to the latest intelligence,

497
23:08.420 --> 23:09.820
Chiang Kai-shek has made

498
23:09.860 --> 23:12.320
a plan to annihilate us in southern Sichuan.

499
23:12.340 --> 23:13.290
Now all his units

500
23:13.450 --> 23:16.310
are gathering on the west bank of the Chishui River.

501
23:19.340 --> 23:21.100
Any movements from the Yunnan Army?

502
23:21.100 --> 23:22.800
Sun Du's column of the Yunnan Army

503
23:22.800 --> 23:24.180
is stationed along the Bijie line.

504
23:24.180 --> 23:25.440
No unusual movements.

505
23:27.770 --> 23:29.170
It seems Chiang Kai-shek

506
23:29.580 --> 23:30.840
is still holding back.

507
23:31.010 --> 23:32.490
We need to make him more confident in his prediction.

508
23:32.490 --> 23:33.800
We must set the rules for him,

509
23:33.800 --> 23:35.860
making him firmly move all his troops

510
23:36.140 --> 23:37.210
to southern Sichuan.

511
23:37.210 --> 23:38.050
It looks like

512
23:38.210 --> 23:40.730
Comrade Zedong already has a good plan.

513
23:41.010 --> 23:42.070
Order the 1st Corps

514
23:42.490 --> 23:44.620
to send a regiment disguised as the main force,

515
23:44.620 --> 23:46.470
posturing to cross the Yangtze River to the north.

516
23:46.470 --> 23:47.600
Make a big show of it.

517
23:47.940 --> 23:48.870
Put on a full act.

518
23:49.100 --> 23:49.660
Okay.

519
23:49.820 --> 23:51.770
The Military Commission and the main forces of all corps

520
23:51.770 --> 23:53.250
must immediately turn back east,

521
23:53.250 --> 23:55.010
secretly, swiftly,

522
23:55.010 --> 23:57.580
and resolutely gather on the west bank of the Chishui River,

523
23:57.580 --> 24:00.490
preparing to cross the Chishui River east again

524
24:00.730 --> 24:02.940
around Erlangtan and Lintan.

525
24:07.770 --> 24:09.770
What a great feint to the west and attack to the east.

526
24:09.770 --> 24:10.490
Mao.

527
24:10.690 --> 24:11.690
This leap of yours

528
24:12.290 --> 24:13.450
seems casual,

529
24:13.580 --> 24:16.100
but has actually been brewing for a long time.

530
24:16.100 --> 24:17.340
Just seeking survival in danger.

531
24:17.340 --> 24:19.470
We have the Yangtze River to the north,

532
24:19.530 --> 24:20.670
the Wujiang River to the south,

533
24:20.670 --> 24:22.180
and the Hengjiang and Jinsha Rivers to the west.

534
24:22.180 --> 24:24.010
The enemy outnumbers us ten to one.

535
24:24.010 --> 24:26.420
If Chiang had left us a way out,

536
24:26.440 --> 24:28.300
we wouldn't be in this situation.

537
24:29.310 --> 24:30.570
Leaders, come wash up.

538
24:30.730 --> 24:31.380
Okay.

539
24:31.530 --> 24:32.050
Come.

540
24:33.490 --> 24:35.020
The earth is our washbasin.

541
25:17.900 --> 25:19.500
The struggle against nature

542
25:20.050 --> 25:21.820
brings endless joy!

543
25:39.770 --> 25:41.370
The struggle against nature

544
25:41.530 --> 25:43.710
brings endless joy!

545
26:49.100 --> 26:50.880
Bamboo clappers ring, loud and clear.

546
26:50.880 --> 26:52.620
The Central Red Army marches far and wide.

547
26:52.620 --> 26:54.450
Crossing over mountains, we're not afraid of hardship;

548
26:54.450 --> 26:56.490
Wading through rivers, we're not afraid of trials.

549
26:56.490 --> 26:58.140
Bamboo clappers ring, look ahead.

550
26:58.140 --> 27:00.010
The road of revolution lies before us.

551
27:00.010 --> 27:01.820
Winter will pass sooner or later;

552
27:01.820 --> 27:03.620
When spring comes, the mountain flowers will bloom red.

553
27:03.620 --> 27:05.290
Comrades, work hard.

554
27:05.310 --> 27:06.940
Keep the Party's orders in mind.

555
27:06.940 --> 27:08.660
Parting today is hard to bear;

556
27:08.690 --> 27:12.140
One day, victory reports will redden the sky.

557
27:15.700 --> 27:18.140
Comrades, cheer up.

558
27:21.390 --> 27:23.430
Everyone, march to the orders.

559
27:26.010 --> 27:26.940
Map.

560
27:36.310 --> 27:38.250
The location designated by the Military Commission

561
27:38.250 --> 27:40.620
should be just over this mountain.

562
27:40.970 --> 27:42.210
It should take about 2 hours.

563
27:42.210 --> 27:43.740
We should have enough time.

564
27:43.770 --> 27:44.500
We have time.

565
27:53.080 --> 27:54.360
Troops, halt.

566
27:57.370 --> 27:58.550
About-face!

567
28:00.620 --> 28:01.620
The lead soldier.

568
28:02.050 --> 28:03.210
Put away the flag.

569
28:04.770 --> 28:06.290
Forward, march.

570
28:09.930 --> 28:10.820
Comrades.

571
28:11.580 --> 28:12.660
Let's sing a song.

572
28:13.450 --> 28:15.710
♪ The revolutionary tide is rising high ♪

573
28:15.900 --> 28:17.710
Ready, go!

574
28:18.040 --> 28:20.670
♪ The revolutionary tide is rising high ♪

575
28:20.730 --> 28:23.290
♪ Workers, peasants, and soldiers unite ♪

576
28:23.380 --> 28:28.100
♪ We workers join with the peasants to make revolution ♪

577
28:28.100 --> 28:30.660
♪ This is our new mission ♪

578
28:30.940 --> 28:33.340
♪ We fear no death, we seek no wealth ♪

579
28:33.530 --> 28:36.190
♪ Together, we press forward with all our might ♪

580
28:46.000 --> 28:48.660
Send a telegram from here and it'll get through.

581
28:53.890 --> 28:54.610
Done.

582
28:54.640 --> 28:55.570
Reel in the line.

583
29:10.940 --> 29:11.750
Move out.

584
29:17.460 --> 29:18.820
Troops, halt.

585
29:18.970 --> 29:20.180
Halt.

586
29:20.780 --> 29:22.100
About-face!

587
29:23.050 --> 29:23.900
Comrades.

588
29:24.210 --> 29:25.180
Double time, march.

589
29:25.180 --> 29:26.420
Hurry, hurry.

590
29:26.450 --> 29:27.210
Double time, march.

591
29:27.210 --> 29:27.740
Run, run.

592
29:27.750 --> 29:28.460
Hurry!

593
29:43.510 --> 29:44.440
Generalissimo.

594
29:45.530 --> 29:47.340
Aerial reconnaissance just reported

595
29:47.340 --> 29:48.340
that a large Communist army force

596
29:48.340 --> 29:50.210
is heading towards Gulin and Xuyong.

597
29:50.210 --> 29:51.380
They are moving in such a hurry

598
29:51.380 --> 29:52.660
that they don't even avoid

599
29:52.660 --> 29:54.260
our reconnaissance planes.

600
29:54.820 --> 29:55.810
Good.

601
29:57.290 --> 29:59.890
The great cause of suppressing the Communists

602
30:01.050 --> 30:02.210
depends on this single move.

603
30:02.210 --> 30:03.010
Yes, sir.

604
30:04.100 --> 30:06.160
On March 20, 1935,

605
30:06.670 --> 30:07.940
Chiang Kai-shek issued a telegram order

606
30:07.940 --> 30:09.490
to annihilate the Central Red Army

607
30:09.490 --> 30:11.770
in the area southeast of Gulin.

608
30:12.380 --> 30:13.690
He strictly ordered hundreds of thousands of Kuomintang troops

609
30:13.690 --> 30:15.030
from Sichuan, Yunnan, and Guizhou,

610
30:15.030 --> 30:18.340
as well as the Central Army, to swarm into southern Sichuan

611
30:18.690 --> 30:20.690
to encircle and block the main force of the Red Army

612
30:20.690 --> 30:21.890
advancing westward.

613
30:22.180 --> 30:23.310
He also claimed that

614
30:23.520 --> 30:27.100
the westward flight of the remnant "bandits" was the only good opportunity for his army.

615
30:27.100 --> 30:28.670
If they could not be annihilated this time,

616
30:28.670 --> 30:31.140
he would have no face to stand in this world.

617
30:31.770 --> 30:32.820
At the same time,

618
30:33.290 --> 30:35.180
the Central Revolutionary Military Commission issued

619
30:35.180 --> 30:36.110
the "Action Plan for the Red Army's

620
30:36.110 --> 30:38.440
Fourth Crossing of the Chishui River".

621
30:40.010 --> 30:42.470
From the night of March 21 to 22,

622
30:43.010 --> 30:45.690
having secretly assembled on the west bank of the Chishui River,

623
30:45.690 --> 30:47.820
the main forces of the Central Red Army

624
30:47.970 --> 30:50.690
quickly and covertly crossed from Erlangtan,

625
30:50.690 --> 30:53.050
Jiuxikou, Taipingdu, and other ferries,

626
30:53.070 --> 30:56.330
to the east of the Chishui River for the fourth time,

627
30:56.660 --> 30:58.480
leaving hundreds of thousands of Kuomintang troops

628
30:58.480 --> 31:00.370
behind in southern Sichuan.

629
31:08.010 --> 31:09.060
Speed up.

630
31:09.350 --> 31:10.420
Stay safe.

631
31:16.530 --> 31:17.440
Stay safe.

632
31:40.070 --> 31:40.760
Enlai.

633
31:41.690 --> 31:42.890
Going back and forth,

634
31:43.830 --> 31:46.690
even the fish in the Chishui River recognize us now.

635
31:48.040 --> 31:50.280
Yes, 4 times.

636
32:02.530 --> 32:05.010
Twenty-five years later, in 1960,

637
32:05.420 --> 32:07.010
when someone highly praised Mao Zedong's

638
32:07.010 --> 32:08.450
art of command during the War of Liberation

639
32:08.450 --> 32:10.900
in the three major campaigns,

640
32:11.060 --> 32:12.450
Mao Zedong said that

641
32:12.470 --> 32:13.700
the Four Crossings of the Chishui River

642
32:13.700 --> 32:16.020
was his proudest masterpiece.

643
32:16.340 --> 32:17.080
Later,

644
32:17.310 --> 32:19.530
General Xiao Hua, who personally experienced the Long March,

645
32:19.530 --> 32:21.910
wrote in the "Long March Suite":

646
32:22.170 --> 32:24.420
Four crossings of the Chishui River, with troops striking unexpectedly;

647
32:24.420 --> 32:27.350
Chairman Mao is truly a master of military strategy.

648
32:44.530 --> 32:46.390
There is no Communist army ahead.

649
32:46.550 --> 32:47.310
It's safe.

650
32:55.350 --> 32:56.910
Rest in place.

651
33:03.720 --> 33:05.480
Sir, when do we eat?

652
33:06.050 --> 33:07.310
All you know is eating.

653
33:07.520 --> 33:08.250
Give it to me.

654
33:22.420 --> 33:24.660
I would like to ask you all a question.

655
33:25.530 --> 33:27.990
The Communist army has less than 30,000 men.

656
33:28.180 --> 33:29.410
On the Chishui River,

657
33:30.280 --> 33:32.910
they swaggered back and forth 4 times.

658
33:33.530 --> 33:34.530
And what about us?

659
33:35.050 --> 33:36.620
We have hundreds of thousands of men

660
33:36.620 --> 33:38.340
surrounding them from front and back.

661
33:38.340 --> 33:40.470
Why are our results so lackluster?

662
33:40.940 --> 33:42.470
Where are the results?

663
33:48.100 --> 33:49.380
You don't want to talk.

664
33:51.360 --> 33:52.510
Fine.

665
33:53.250 --> 33:54.770
I'll say it for you.

666
33:55.870 --> 33:59.050
Mao Zedong commands his troops as if they were extensions of himself.

667
33:59.050 --> 34:00.050
And what about us?

668
34:00.390 --> 34:02.070
The men on our side all have their own hidden agendas

669
34:02.070 --> 34:04.070
and are divided in their loyalties.

670
34:04.130 --> 34:05.390
Take the Sichuan Army.

671
34:05.730 --> 34:07.420
As long as the Communist army doesn't enter Sichuan,

672
34:07.420 --> 34:09.170
they just go through the motions.

673
34:09.170 --> 34:10.070
And the Yunnan Army.

674
34:10.070 --> 34:12.679
Sun Du and Long Yun echo each other,

675
34:13.380 --> 34:14.780
and just hold their ground.

676
34:14.780 --> 34:17.060
Wang Jialie is more of a hindrance than a help.

677
34:17.060 --> 34:18.820
And what about the Central Army?

678
34:18.820 --> 34:21.090
Of the 2 top generals under Xue Yue of the Central Army,

679
34:21.090 --> 34:22.780
one was scared out of his wits,

680
34:22.860 --> 34:24.860
and the other was beaten senseless.

681
34:25.380 --> 34:26.510
I want to ask you all,

682
34:26.650 --> 34:29.650
when the Communist army crossed east again this time,

683
34:30.380 --> 34:32.300
did you notice it?

684
34:36.100 --> 34:43.250
[Huilong Temple, Xishui, Guizhou]

685
34:42.130 --> 34:43.900
Generalissimo Chiang racked his brains,

686
34:43.900 --> 34:45.650
but every move he made

687
34:45.940 --> 34:47.739
was half a step slower than ours.

688
34:48.610 --> 34:50.340
We are already in northern Guizhou,

689
34:50.340 --> 34:52.110
eating these mutton rice noodles.

690
34:52.110 --> 34:55.130
Their hundreds of thousands of troops are still in southern Sichuan,

691
34:55.130 --> 34:57.010
helping us pull off the empty fort stratagem.

692
34:57.010 --> 34:58.650
Don't underestimate this half step.

693
34:58.650 --> 35:00.220
We suddenly have

694
35:00.240 --> 35:01.290
room to maneuver.

695
35:02.450 --> 35:03.940
We can't keep up the empty fort stratagem

696
35:03.940 --> 35:05.130
for too long.

697
35:05.700 --> 35:08.850
Chiang Kai-shek will soon come to his senses.

698
35:09.330 --> 35:11.830
We absolutely cannot stay in northern Guizhou for long.

699
35:11.830 --> 35:12.720
Let's eat together.

700
35:12.720 --> 35:13.640
Okay.

701
35:16.900 --> 35:18.830
The Communist army's eastward crossing

702
35:18.830 --> 35:20.270
has 2 possibilities.

703
35:21.530 --> 35:23.050
One is to occupy Zunyi

704
35:23.660 --> 35:25.650
and rebuild their base in northern Guizhou,

705
35:25.650 --> 35:27.380
looking for a chance to cross the Yangtze River northward

706
35:27.380 --> 35:29.380
and join forces with Xu Xiangqian's troops.

707
35:29.380 --> 35:31.110
There is another possibility.

708
35:31.220 --> 35:34.010
They might use northern Guizhou as a springboard,

709
35:34.010 --> 35:36.070
cross the Wujiang River to the south,

710
35:36.510 --> 35:37.910
return to western Hunan,

711
35:38.680 --> 35:40.910
and join forces with He Long and Xiao Ke.

712
35:41.740 --> 35:42.700
Gentlemen,

713
35:43.150 --> 35:46.060
I ask you to redeploy your defenses

714
35:46.420 --> 35:48.260
and encircle them tightly.

715
35:48.500 --> 35:51.620
Neither of these 2 possibilities is allowed to happen.

716
35:55.890 --> 35:56.540
Currently,

717
35:56.540 --> 36:00.140
the Sichuan army is guarding the Chishui and Tucheng line.

718
36:00.610 --> 36:01.820
We can't go north.

719
36:02.170 --> 36:03.970
To the east, Shangguan Yunxiang

720
36:04.700 --> 36:06.080
is guarding the Tongzi, Loushanguan,

721
36:06.080 --> 36:07.610
and Zunyi line.

722
36:08.050 --> 36:09.860
We can't go east.

723
36:10.900 --> 36:11.610
To the west,

724
36:11.900 --> 36:13.140
there are those we just shook off,

725
36:13.140 --> 36:14.600
Zhou Hunyuan and Wu Qiwei.

726
36:14.650 --> 36:16.220
They will return soon

727
36:16.610 --> 36:18.550
and set up defenses along the Chishui River.

728
36:18.550 --> 36:19.430
We have no way to cross

729
36:19.430 --> 36:20.510
to the west either.

730
36:23.680 --> 36:24.810
Listen to my orders.

731
36:28.380 --> 36:30.050
Order Shangguan Yunxiang's troops

732
36:30.050 --> 36:31.890
to set up defenses along the Sichuan-Guizhou Highway

733
36:31.890 --> 36:34.600
at Tongzi, Songkan, Loushanguan,

734
36:34.820 --> 36:35.900
and Zunyi.

735
36:36.020 --> 36:38.090
Zhou Hunyuan's column and Wu Qiwei's column

736
36:38.090 --> 36:39.860
will set up defenses along the Renhuai, Maotai,

737
36:39.860 --> 36:41.260
and Tanchang line.

738
36:41.340 --> 36:43.360
Order Zhou Hunyuan to dispatch 3 full regiments

739
36:43.360 --> 36:46.740
to hold the line at Yaxi, Bailakan, and Fengxiangba

740
36:46.820 --> 36:47.970
firmly.

741
36:49.300 --> 36:50.300
Telegraph He Jian

742
36:50.420 --> 36:51.740
to hold the Wujiang River defense line.

743
36:51.740 --> 36:53.780
The Communist army must never be allowed to cross the Wujiang River.

744
36:53.780 --> 36:55.090
Reporting, Generalissimo!

745
36:55.090 --> 36:55.530
Speak.

746
36:55.820 --> 36:56.950
Those who know shame

747
36:57.190 --> 36:59.150
advance quickly.

748
36:59.530 --> 37:01.420
If a man knows shame,

749
37:01.740 --> 37:03.450
he will rise up in indignation.

750
37:03.450 --> 37:04.130
We will

751
37:04.830 --> 37:07.870
learn from our shame and fight bravely.

752
37:22.190 --> 37:23.110
Gentlemen,

753
37:23.320 --> 37:25.130
I will go with you

754
37:25.550 --> 37:26.630
to Guizhou.

755
37:27.290 --> 37:29.550
I will personally supervise the battle.

756
37:30.260 --> 37:31.790
I want you all to understand

757
37:31.900 --> 37:33.820
that this is our final showdown against

758
37:33.820 --> 37:35.450
the Zhu-Mao Communist army.

759
37:36.220 --> 37:38.830
The success or failure of the great cause of suppressing the communists

760
37:38.830 --> 37:40.250
depends on this one action!

761
37:40.250 --> 37:41.430
Yes, sir!

762
37:46.090 --> 37:47.170
We can't go north,

763
37:47.570 --> 37:48.700
east,

764
37:49.050 --> 37:50.260
or west.

765
37:50.510 --> 37:51.540
The only way left is south.

766
37:51.540 --> 37:52.460
Going south

767
37:52.970 --> 37:54.030
is the only way out.

768
37:54.420 --> 37:56.900
It seems that our previously formulated plan

769
37:56.900 --> 37:59.940
to create a new Soviet area on the borders of Sichuan, Yunnan, and Guizhou

770
37:59.940 --> 38:02.000
will be very difficult to implement.

771
38:03.380 --> 38:04.780
Lose land to save people.

772
38:04.940 --> 38:06.470
Let's seek survival first.

773
38:09.060 --> 38:11.810
The problem is, there's only so much ground in northern Guizhou.

774
38:11.810 --> 38:13.600
How can our corps go south

775
38:13.860 --> 38:15.260
without being noticed?

776
38:22.050 --> 38:23.110
Have the 9th Corps,

777
38:24.820 --> 38:25.880
our light cavalry,

778
38:26.210 --> 38:28.090
continue to disguise themselves as the main force of the Red Army

779
38:28.090 --> 38:28.490
and move north,

780
38:28.490 --> 38:30.340
towards Liangcun

781
38:30.610 --> 38:32.410
and Xinglongchang in the north.

782
38:32.530 --> 38:35.130
to cover the covert movement of our main force.

783
38:36.270 --> 38:38.930
Make a feint to the north and attack in the south.

784
38:44.790 --> 38:45.370
Comrade Zedong.

785
38:45.370 --> 38:47.170
Don't you know I don't eat chili?

786
38:48.260 --> 38:49.050
It packs a punch.

787
38:49.050 --> 38:49.650
Here.

788
38:50.340 --> 38:52.260
Even if I eat more chili peppers, I still can't come up with that...

789
38:52.260 --> 38:54.320
feinting north and attacking south.

790
38:54.560 --> 38:55.310
Eat more.

791
38:55.780 --> 38:56.970
You'll like it if you eat more.

792
38:56.970 --> 38:57.590
Okay.

793
38:57.790 --> 38:58.650
I'll have some.

794
39:05.120 --> 39:06.160
Come on.

795
39:16.590 --> 39:20.950
["Hot Wind" by Lu Xun]

796
39:29.740 --> 39:31.000
Give off as much warmth

797
39:31.010 --> 39:32.140
and light as you can.

798
39:32.490 --> 39:33.820
Even like a firefly,

799
39:34.290 --> 39:36.690
you can shed a little light in the darkness.

800
39:36.900 --> 39:38.620
There is no need to wait for a torch to appear.

801
39:38.620 --> 39:40.820
If, in the end, no torch should appear,

802
39:39.420 --> 39:42.370
[Wei Yueqiao, Staff of the 2nd Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

803
39:41.220 --> 39:42.650
then I shall be the only light.

804
39:42.650 --> 39:43.450
Wei Yueqiao.

805
39:43.940 --> 39:45.800
Was this written by Chairman Mao?

806
39:46.220 --> 39:47.820
It's an article by Mr. Lu Xun.

807
39:47.940 --> 39:49.880
Chairman Mao really likes this passage.

808
39:49.880 --> 39:50.880
How do you know?

809
39:51.400 --> 39:52.460
Pass me the hammer.

810
39:52.710 --> 39:54.200
I know the Chairman very well.

811
39:54.200 --> 39:54.910
Really?

812
39:55.780 --> 39:57.300
When he was working in Yeping,

813
39:57.300 --> 39:58.500
he lived in our house.

814
39:58.780 --> 40:00.170
Mr. Lu Xun's collection of essays

815
40:00.170 --> 40:01.840
was recommended to me by the Chairman.

816
40:01.840 --> 40:04.840
He also influenced me to take the revolutionary path.

817
40:05.010 --> 40:05.610
By the way,

818
40:05.940 --> 40:06.780
did you know?

819
40:06.800 --> 40:08.970
When I was teaching at Lenin Primary School,

820
40:08.970 --> 40:10.650
the Chairman even attended my class.

821
40:10.650 --> 40:11.650
At that time, the Chairman said,

822
40:11.650 --> 40:12.450
"Wei Yueqiao,

823
40:12.740 --> 40:14.000
you are a little teacher.

824
40:14.000 --> 40:15.400
I used to be a teacher too.

825
40:15.450 --> 40:17.530
So we are colleagues."

826
40:18.810 --> 40:19.480
Yueqiao.

827
40:19.900 --> 40:21.630
Listening to the passage you just read,

828
40:21.630 --> 40:24.160
I felt it resonated deeply with Chairman Mao.

829
40:24.490 --> 40:25.350
Think about it.

830
40:25.970 --> 40:27.380
In our most difficult

831
40:27.580 --> 40:28.630
and darkest times,

832
40:28.630 --> 40:30.750
isn't Chairman Mao like our light?

833
40:31.340 --> 40:32.140
That's right.

834
40:32.300 --> 40:34.550
Chairman Mao is that light.

835
40:35.740 --> 40:36.820
That light ignited

836
40:37.230 --> 40:38.830
you and me,

837
40:39.420 --> 40:40.750
and so many more lights.

838
40:40.790 --> 40:42.860
When all the lights gather together,

839
40:43.570 --> 40:45.740
the road ahead will be bright.

840
40:45.830 --> 40:46.940
Well said.

841
40:48.010 --> 40:49.870
You are amazing, little teacher.

842
40:50.540 --> 40:51.150
Director.

843
40:51.580 --> 40:52.940
I was just expressing my feelings.

844
40:52.940 --> 40:54.270
Your feelings

845
40:54.860 --> 40:56.220
touched our hearts.

846
40:56.860 --> 40:58.450
The harder the times,

847
40:58.510 --> 41:01.310
the more we need all the lights to gather together.

848
41:01.860 --> 41:04.170
A few days ago, you and the 6th Red Regiment

849
41:04.170 --> 41:05.300
went to Gulin to lure the enemy.

850
41:05.230 --> 41:08.730
[Zeng Xisheng, Director of the Second Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

851
41:05.410 --> 41:06.860
You completed the task very well.

852
41:06.860 --> 41:08.940
The Military Commission praised your work.

853
41:08.940 --> 41:09.700
Really?

854
41:10.130 --> 41:11.300
Since I performed so well,

855
41:11.300 --> 41:12.570
can I join the Decryption Section?

856
41:12.570 --> 41:14.090
You really want to do decryption?

857
41:14.090 --> 41:14.220
I...

858
41:14.220 --> 41:15.010
About this,

859
41:15.330 --> 41:17.060
even the mules pulling the generators in our Second Bureau

860
41:17.060 --> 41:18.020
know about it.

861
41:18.050 --> 41:19.130
Exactly.

862
41:23.150 --> 41:23.980
Wei.

863
41:24.210 --> 41:26.010
You want to go to the Decryption Section.

864
41:26.010 --> 41:27.010
I don't object.

865
41:27.340 --> 41:28.720
But right now, our Second Bureau

866
41:28.720 --> 41:30.190
has another important task

867
41:30.190 --> 41:31.990
that needs someone to complete.

868
41:32.570 --> 41:33.450
Qian and I

869
41:33.480 --> 41:35.620
[Qian Zhuangfei, Deputy Director of the Second Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

870
41:33.550 --> 41:34.680
have considered it.

871
41:34.770 --> 41:37.570
We agree that you are the most suitable candidate.

872
41:38.220 --> 41:38.940
What task?

873
41:38.960 --> 41:41.540
The Military Commission requires our Second Bureau to send a comrade

874
41:41.540 --> 41:42.530
to the 9th Corps

875
41:42.700 --> 41:44.180
to act with them.

876
41:44.530 --> 41:45.860
To strengthen the 9th Corps'

877
41:45.860 --> 41:47.570
technical reconnaissance and communication work.

878
41:47.570 --> 41:48.780
Then I have to leave the Second Bureau?

879
41:48.780 --> 41:49.610
That's right.

880
41:50.340 --> 41:51.280
The mission of the 9th Corps

881
41:51.280 --> 41:53.300
is to cover the main force's movement.

882
41:53.300 --> 41:56.100
It directly concerns the safety of the main force.

883
41:58.570 --> 41:59.770
Comrade Wei Yueqiao.

884
42:00.300 --> 42:01.170
I promise you,

885
42:01.410 --> 42:02.860
once you complete this mission,

886
42:02.860 --> 42:04.760
I will personally submit a report to the Military Commission

887
42:04.760 --> 42:06.530
to transfer you back to the Second Bureau.

888
42:06.530 --> 42:08.860
Yes. I guarantee to complete the mission.

889
42:10.300 --> 42:10.860
Good.

890
42:11.010 --> 42:11.820
Wei.

891
42:12.340 --> 42:14.610
I happen to be going to the Military Commission for a meeting.

892
42:14.610 --> 42:15.650
Help me pack up,

893
42:16.130 --> 42:17.390
and we'll go together.

894
42:17.630 --> 42:18.380
Yes, sir.

895
42:18.400 --> 42:19.090
Come.

896
42:20.900 --> 42:21.560
Go ahead.

897
42:24.590 --> 42:25.700
Comrade Zhuangfei.

898
42:25.700 --> 42:26.670
I heard from Director Zou

899
42:26.670 --> 42:28.990
that you've been transferred to the General Political Department.

900
42:28.990 --> 42:29.590
Yes.

901
42:29.870 --> 42:31.380
After the Zunyi Conference,

902
42:31.380 --> 42:33.110
I received the transfer order.

903
42:35.200 --> 42:36.150
Then in the Second Bureau from now on,

904
42:36.150 --> 42:38.080
we won't be able to see you anymore?

905
42:39.130 --> 42:40.660
Won't get to see me anymore?

906
42:41.700 --> 42:43.650
Even if I go to the General Political Department,

907
42:43.650 --> 42:46.310
aren't we all still in the Military Commission?

908
42:46.780 --> 42:49.510
There will always be chances to meet if we want to.

909
42:49.530 --> 42:51.050
When will that be?

910
42:52.390 --> 42:53.320
Miss me already?

911
42:58.340 --> 42:59.450
Comrade Zhuangfei.

912
42:59.450 --> 43:02.260
Could you write a few parting words for me?

913
43:02.450 --> 43:03.220
Sure.
